# go-common Agent Context

## Purpose
Shared Go utility library for all STECH services. **PUBLIC REPO** — never commit secrets.

## Module
```
github.com/STECH-Super-App/go-common
```

## Package Reference

| Package | Key Exports | Used For |
|---------|-------------|----------|
| `pkg/auth` | `Claims`, `HeaderUserID/Role/Name/Type/TenantID` | JWT claims, auth header constants |
| `pkg/config` | `Init()`, `GetEnv()`, `GetEnvInt/Bool/Duration()` | Env var loading from `.env` |
| `pkg/db` | `NewPostgres(ctx, cfg)`, `NewRedis(ctx, cfg)` | DB connection factories |
| `pkg/errors` | `AppError`, `BadRequest/NotFound/Unauthorized/Forbidden/InternalServerError()` | Standardized HTTP errors |
| `pkg/logger` | `New(level, service) (*zap.Logger, error)`, `IntoContext`/`FromContext` | Structured JSON logging (JSON encoder unconditional) + request-scoped logger on `context.Context` |
| `pkg/metrics` | `Registry`, `MountOn(e)`, `StartServer(addr)`, `HTTPRequestDuration`, `GRPCServerHandling`, `DefaultBuckets`, `StatusClass`, `NewCounter/Gauge/Histogram()` | Prometheus instruments + `/metrics` exposition |
| `pkg/middleware` | `CORS()`, `Tracing()`, `RequestLogger()`, `Metrics()`, `MetricsUnaryServerInterceptor()`, `AuthMiddleware()`, `UserIDFromContext()` | HTTP middlewares, gRPC interceptors, context helpers (`Logger()` deprecated → `RequestLogger()`) |
| `pkg/input` | `Line()`, `Body()`, `Required()`, `UUID()`, `Int32/Int64()`, `ParseInt32/ParseInt64()`, `ParsePage()`, `MaxItems()`, `Phone()`, `Email()`, `Failure` (`At`, `AtPage`), `Collect()`, `GRPC()`, `MessageFor()`, `Reason*` | Input validation returning the CLEANED value; status-free `COMMON_*` Reasons; text rule mirrors sale-service `ControlCharacters` |
| `pkg/db/pgerr` | `InvalidInput(err) (*input.Failure, bool)` | Repository backstop (22021/22P05/22001/22P02 + pgx int encode) — first line of every `mapPgError`; meters `stech_input_backstop_total{sqlstate}` |
| `pkg/utils` | `Ptr()`, `ToVal()`, `Contains()`, `Map()`, `Filter()` | Generic utilities |
| `pkg/health` | Health check endpoint | Service health monitoring |
| `pkg/client` | gRPC client utilities | Service-to-service communication |
| `pkg/outbox` | `New()`, `Start()`, `PublishProto()`, `RunInTx()`, `DBTX`, `Migrate()`, `Deduplicator`, `Store.PendingStats()`, `ExtractOutboxID()`, `ExtractEventType()` | Transactional outbox pattern (at-least-once Kafka delivery + consumer dedup), backlog metrics, `traceparent` capture |
| `pkg/notifyrender` | `BaselineEN`, `RequiredParams()`, `OptionalParams()`, `ExtractParams()`, `Render()` | The in-app/push notification catalogue: EN baselines per type, the required/optional param tiers, the per-payload extract arms (a protoreflect completeness test reds a declared field no arm reads), the i18n-catalog overlay contract |
| `pkg/notifyoutbox` | `PublishDirective()` | Writes a notification directive into the caller's outbox transaction after three in-tx checks: envelope shape, required params, and (for `REPAIR_*`) the exact `[IN_APP, PUSH]` channel set — an unknown type or a missing required param rolls the caller's write back |
| `pkg/tracing` | `Init(serviceName) (shutdown, error)` | OpenTelemetry setup; no-op + nil error when `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` is unset |

## Context Keys (pkg/middleware)
`ContextKeyUserID`, `ContextKeyUserRole`, `ContextKeyUserName`, `ContextKeyUserType`, `ContextKeyTenantID`

## Observability contract (Wave 0, 2026-08-25)
- Every instrument registers on `metrics.Registry` **at package init**, never inside a middleware factory or server constructor — service tests rebuild those repeatedly in one process and `MustRegister` panics on the second call. `promauto` and the prometheus default registerer are forbidden: nothing serves them.
- Allowed metric label keys fleet-wide: `method, route, status_class, grpc_service, grpc_method, grpc_code, topic, group, reason, vertical, sqlstate` (`sqlstate` = pgerr's closed five-value set). Never ids, raw paths, emails or tokens. The same law governs span names.
- Duration buckets are fixed at `[0.005, 0.01, 0.025, 0.05, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2.5, 5, 10]`.
- Operational routes `/metrics`, `/health`, `/livez`, `/readyz` are skipped by every observability middleware; an unmatched route clamps to `unmatched`.
- Tracing must be absence-tolerant: no OTLP endpoint means a no-op provider and a nil error. Observability must never be able to take a service down.
- The outbox `traceparent` is captured at insert time from the producing request's context — never at relay time, which would root every trace at the relay process.

## Critical Rules
- This is a PUBLIC repo — never add secrets, credentials, or internal URLs
- All services depend on this — breaking changes affect everything
- After pushing changes: run `./update_go_common.sh` from monorepo root
